// OMF - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# The Object Module Format, used by Microsoft's 16-bit toolchain.
# An OMF record starts with a one-byte record type and ends with a
# one-byte checksum: the ones complement of the record's byte sum.
#
# 0x8E is THEADR, a translation-unit header. The name below is the one
# a linker would report for the module.
0000  8C 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21 00 35    |.Hello World!.5|
